  "note": "海崖口、海崖道、崖脚 (native:fanfang/cliff_top, cliff_path, cliff_foot; 番坊 A): the path from 忘情谷's woods comes out on a bare headland of grey-green turf, and the sea shows at last, far below to the west — grey-blue to the sky's edge, the surf white at the cliffs' foot; a road cut into the dark sea cliff runs south along a low lip of rock, wet and worn to a shine by the salt porters, stone steps cut where it drops; the sea god's niche on the headland with shells and a coin before it, a cairn, gulls wheeling below the road, salt spray blowing up over the lip; at the foot a bench and the steps down, the port's roofs far down to the south-east. Old and used: steps worn hollow, salt crusted on the rock, a porters' resting place.",
